A. SSTF – Shortest Seek Time First
1. Aim
To implement SSTF disk scheduling algorithm and calculate total head movement.
2. Code Explanation
Step 1: Header Files
#include<stdio.h>
#include<stdlib.h>


- stdio.h – Input/output.
- stdlib.h – Provides abs() function.
Step 2: Declare Variables
int RQ[100], i, n, TotalHeadMoment=0, initial, count=0;


- RQ[100] – Stores disk requests.
- n – Number of requests.
- initial – Initial head position.
- TotalHeadMoment – Total head movement.
- count – Number of completed requests.
Step 3: Take Input
scanf("%d",&n);

for(i=0;i<n;i++)
    scanf("%d",&RQ[i]);

scanf("%d",&initial);


Takes number of requests, request sequence and initial head position.

Step 4: Find Nearest Request
Most Important
while(count!=n)
{
    int min=1000,d,index;

    for(i=0;i<n;i++)
    {
        d=abs(RQ[i]-initial);

        if(min>d)
        {
            min=d;
            index=i;
        }
    }


- while(count!=n) – Runs until all requests complete.
- min=1000 – Initial minimum distance.
- abs() – Calculates positive distance.
- d – Distance between current head and request.
- if(min>d) – Checks nearest request.
- index – Stores nearest request position.
Step 5: Update Head Movement
TotalHeadMoment=TotalHeadMoment+min;

initial=RQ[index];

RQ[index]=1000;

count++;


- Adds minimum distance to total movement.
- Moves head to selected request.
- RQ[index]=1000 – Marks request as completed.
- count++ – Increases completed request count.
Step 6: Display Output
printf("Total head movement is %d",TotalHeadMoment);


Displays total head movement.
