B. SCAN – Disk Scheduling
1. Aim
To implement SCAN disk scheduling algorithm and calculate total head movement.
2. Code Explanation
Step 1: Declare Variables
int RQ[100], i, j, n;
int TotalHeadMoment=0, initial, size, move;


- RQ[] – Stores requests.
- n – Number of requests.
- initial – Initial head position.
- size – Total disk size.
- move – Direction of head movement.
- TotalHeadMoment – Total movement.
Step 2: Take Input
scanf("%d",&n);

for(i=0;i<n;i++)
    scanf("%d",&RQ[i]);

scanf("%d",&initial);
scanf("%d",&size);
scanf("%d",&move);


Inputs:
- Number of requests.
- Request sequence.
- Initial head position.
- Disk size.
- Direction: 1 for high, 0 for low.
Step 3: Sort Request Array
for(i=0;i<n;i++)
{
    for(j=0;j<n-i-1;j++)
    {
        if(RQ[j]>RQ[j+1])
        {
            int temp;
            temp=RQ[j];
            RQ[j]=RQ[j+1];
            RQ[j+1]=temp;
        }
    }
}


- Sorts requests in ascending order.
- Uses Bubble Sort.
- temp – Temporarily stores value during swapping.
Step 4: Find Index
int index;

for(i=0;i<n;i++)
{
    if(initial<RQ[i])
    {
        index=i;
        break;
    }
}


- Finds first request greater than initial head.
- index – Stores its position.
Step 5: Movement Towards High
if(move==1)
{
    for(i=index;i<n;i++)
    {
        TotalHeadMoment += abs(RQ[i]-initial);
        initial=RQ[i];
    }

    TotalHeadMoment += abs(size-RQ[i-1]-1);
    initial=size-1;


- move==1 – Head moves towards higher values.
- Services requests in ascending order.
- Moves to last disk position (size-1).
Step 6: Return Towards Low
for(i=index-1;i>=0;i--)
{
    TotalHeadMoment += abs(RQ[i]-initial);
    initial=RQ[i];
}


Services remaining requests in descending order.

Step 7: Movement Towards Low
else
{
    for(i=index-1;i>=0;i--)
    {
        TotalHeadMoment += abs(RQ[i]-initial);
        initial=RQ[i];
    }

    TotalHeadMoment += abs(RQ[i+1]-0);
    initial=0;


- move==0 – Head moves towards lower values.
- Services lower requests.
- Moves to disk position 0.
Step 8: Services Remaining Requests
for(i=index;i<n;i++)
{
    TotalHeadMoment += abs(RQ[i]-initial);
    initial=RQ[i];
}


Services remaining higher requests.

Step 9: Display
printf("Total head movement is %d",TotalHeadMoment);


Displays total movement.
