C. C-LOOK – Circular LOOK Disk Scheduling
1. Aim
To implement C-LOOK disk scheduling algorithm and calculate total head movement.
2. Code Explanation
Step 1: Declare Variables
int RQ[100], i, j, n;
int TotalHeadMoment=0, initial, size, move;


- RQ[] – Stores requests.
- n – Number of requests.
- initial – Initial head position.
- size – Disk size.
- move – Direction.
- TotalHeadMoment – Total movement.
Step 2: Take Input
scanf("%d",&n);

for(i=0;i<n;i++)
    scanf("%d",&RQ[i]);

scanf("%d",&initial);
scanf("%d",&size);
scanf("%d",&move);


Takes requests, initial head position, disk size and direction.

Step 3: Sort Requests
for(i=0;i<n;i++)
{
    for(j=0;j<n-i-1;j++)
    {
        if(RQ[j]>RQ[j+1])
        {
            int temp;
            temp=RQ[j];
            RQ[j]=RQ[j+1];
            RQ[j+1]=temp;
        }
    }
}


Sorts all requests in ascending order using Bubble Sort.

Step 4: Find Index
int index;

for(i=0;i<n;i++)
{
    if(initial<RQ[i])
    {
        index=i;
        break;
    }
}


Finds the first request greater than initial head position.

Step 5: Movement Towards High
Most Important
if(move==1)
{
    for(i=index;i<n;i++)
    {
        TotalHeadMoment += abs(RQ[i]-initial);
        initial=RQ[i];
    }

    for(i=0;i<index;i++)
    {
        TotalHeadMoment += abs(RQ[i]-initial);
        initial=RQ[i];
    }
}


- move==1 – Moves towards higher values.
- First loop – Services higher requests.
- Second loop – Jumps to lowest request and services remaining requests.
- Does not travel to the physical end of the disk.
Step 6: Movement Towards Low
else
{
    for(i=index-1;i>=0;i--)
    {
        TotalHeadMoment += abs(RQ[i]-initial);
        initial=RQ[i];
    }

    for(i=n-1;i>=index;i--)
    {
        TotalHeadMoment += abs(RQ[i]-initial);
        initial=RQ[i];
    }
}


- move==0 – Moves towards lower values.
- First loop – Services lower requests.
- Second loop – Jumps to highest request and services remaining requests in descending order.
Step 7: Display
printf("Total head movement is %d",TotalHeadMoment);


Displays total head movement.
